    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Goal: Rank incoming AI research papers for relevance to an applied AI engineer focused on agents, RAG, evals, reliability, orchestration, and production AI.\nModel: claude-sonnet-4-6\nPrompt version: baseline_v2_temp0\nTemperature: 0\nOutput: integer relevance score 0–10 plus concise reason.\nProduction threshold: score >= 6\nWhy threshold 6: False negatives are more costly than false positives for this use case; the user would rather skim an occasional marginal paper than miss a genuinely useful one.\nDevelopment set: Golden Set, 30 manually labeled papers. This set was used while improving the scoring prompt, so it is development data rather than a clean test set.\nInitial untouched Test Set result at threshold 7: 30 papers; TP 3, FP 0, FN 1, TN 26 → precision 100%, recall 75%, accuracy 96.7%.\nObserved FN: SWE Refactor Bench, consistently scored 6.\nScore stability: Across three identical temperature-0 Test Set runs, 27/30 papers received exactly the same score; the remaining three varied by only 1 point. All four human-relevant papers were completely stable.\nFinal threshold-6 result: TP 4, FP 0, FN 0, TN 26 → precision 100%, recall 100%, accuracy 100% on test_set_v1.\nImportant caveat: Because threshold 6 was selected after inspecting Test Set results, the threshold-6 100% result should be viewed as a post-test system decision, not a pristine untouched generalization estimate. The original threshold-7 result is the cleaner held-out evaluation.\nProduction behavior: Papers scoring 6+ proceed to summarization/digest; lower-scoring papers are filtered out. Raw scores, reasons, tokens, model/prompt versions, dataset, and run IDs are logged to Google Sheets.",
